WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.253
Anne had been doing her lessons at home.

2
00:00:06.254 --> 00:00:14.747
One morning, however, Anne came into the kitchen with her schoolbooks and announced, "Marilla, I'm going back to school.

3
00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:19.945
I miss spending time with my best friend Diana, so I must return."

4
00:00:19.946 --> 00:00:26.593
Marilla hid her delight well. "I hope you'll behave yourself," was all she said.

5
00:00:26.594 --> 00:00:32.216
In January the Canadian premier toured Canada, including Prince Edward Island.

6
00:00:32.217 --> 00:00:41.768
Most of Avonlea supported the premier's politics, and many people, including Marilla and Mrs. Lynde, went to hear him speak in Charlottetown.

7
00:00:41.769 --> 00:00:45.237
They planned to return to Green Gables the next day.

8
00:00:45.238 --> 00:00:51.163
So Anne and Matthew had the cheerful, warm kitchen of Green Gables to themselves.

9
00:00:51.164 --> 00:00:55.615
"Matthew, did you ever study geometry?" asked Anne.

10
00:00:55.616 --> 00:00:58.777
"Well, no, I didn't," Matthew said.

11
00:00:58.778 --> 00:01:05.924
"I wish you had," Anne said, "because then you could sympathize. I'm terrible at it!"

12
00:01:05.925 --> 00:01:10.785
Suddenly the kitchen door flung open, and Diana Barry ran in.

13
00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:18.503
"What's the matter, Diana?" cried Anne. "Has your mother changed her mind? Can we be friends again?"

14
00:01:18.504 --> 00:01:22.300
"Oh, Anne, come quickly!" Diana urged her.

15
00:01:22.301 --> 00:01:27.431
"My little sister, Minnie May, is awfully sick—she's got croup.

16
00:01:27.432 --> 00:01:32.921
Father and Mother are in town at the premier's meeting and there's nobody to get the doctor.

17
00:01:32.922 --> 00:01:36.747
The baby-sitter doesn't know what to do, and I'm so scared."

18
00:01:36.748 --> 00:01:40.592
Matthew reached for his cap and went outside to get the horse.

19
00:01:40.593 --> 00:01:47.290
"Matthew will ride to Carmody for the doctor," said Anne. She quickly put on her coat.

20
00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:50.557
"Don't cry, Diana," she went on cheerfully.

21
00:01:50.558 --> 00:01:53.402
"I know exactly what to do for croup.

22
00:01:53.403 --> 00:02:01.431
Mrs. Hammond had twins three times, which gave me lots of experience because they all had croup regularly.

23
00:02:01.432 --> 00:02:05.996
I'll get the ipecac bottle in case you don't have any. Come on."

24
00:02:05.997 --> 00:02:12.430
The two girls hurried to the Barrys' house through the fields, for the snow was too deep to go the shorter way.

25
00:02:12.431 --> 00:02:20.611
Although Anne was sincerely worried about Minnie May, she was delighted to be spending time with Diana again outside of school.

26
00:02:20.612 --> 00:02:26.431
She thought it was truly wonderful to walk through the dark snowy night with her best friend.

27
00:02:26.432 --> 00:02:33.593
At the Barrys', Minnie May was feverish and restless, and her hoarse breathing rattled through the whole house.

28
00:02:33.594 --> 00:02:38.471
Anne promptly went to work. "Minnie May has croup all right.

29
00:02:38.472 --> 00:02:45.111
She's pretty bad, but I've seen worse. First we must have lots of hot water.

30
00:02:45.112 --> 00:02:49.094
Diana, fill up the kettle and put some wood in the stove.

31
00:02:49.095 --> 00:02:52.688
I'll undress Minnie May and give her some ipecac."

32
00:02:52.689 --> 00:02:58.234
The little girl did not take kindly to the ipecac, but Anne kept trying.

33
00:02:58.235 --> 00:03:05.397
She gave Minnie the ipecac many times during the long anxious night, but Minnie got worse.

34
00:03:05.398 --> 00:03:09.387
Anne thought Minnie was sicker than the Hammond twins ever were.

35
00:03:09.388 --> 00:03:14.467
It was difficult for Minnie to breathe, and it seemed like she could choke to death.

36
00:03:14.468 --> 00:03:18.737
Anne, losing hope, gave her the last drop of ipecac.

37
00:03:18.738 --> 00:03:23.995
In a few minutes, Minnie coughed up phlegm and began to get better right away.

38
00:03:23.996 --> 00:03:30.378
She soon fell asleep. It was three o'clock when Matthew finally arrived with the doctor.

39
00:03:30.379 --> 00:03:34.248
"I nearly gave up," Anne said to the doctor.

40
00:03:34.249 --> 00:03:38.545
"You can't imagine my relief when she finally seemed better."

41
00:03:38.546 --> 00:03:41.707
The doctor nodded and went to check on Minnie.

42
00:03:41.708 --> 00:03:46.926
Anne was exhausted from no sleep, and she went home with Matthew.

43
00:03:46.927 --> 00:03:50.690
In the morning Mr. and Mrs. Barry came home.

44
00:03:50.691 --> 00:03:54.472
The doctor, Diana, and Minnie were in the living room.

45
00:03:54.473 --> 00:03:59.896
The doctor told Mr. and Mrs. Barry, "That redheaded girl is a clever thing!

46
00:03:59.897 --> 00:04:02.746
I tell you, she saved that baby's life.

47
00:04:02.747 --> 00:04:06.102
For someone her age, she was smart and calm.

48
00:04:06.103 --> 00:04:09.745
It was wonderful. I've never seen anything like it."

49
00:04:09.746 --> 00:04:13.556
Anne didn't wake up until the evening of the next day.

50
00:04:13.557 --> 00:04:16.969
She went to the kitchen where Marilla sat knitting.

51
00:04:16.970 --> 00:04:21.620
"Anne," Marilla said, "Matthew told me about last night.

52
00:04:21.621 --> 00:04:24.611
It's very fortunate you knew what to do.

53
00:04:24.612 --> 00:04:29.749
I wouldn't have any idea myself, for I never saw a case of croup."

54
00:04:29.750 --> 00:04:33.954
"Mrs. Barry was here this afternoon, Anne," Marilla continued.

55
00:04:33.955 --> 00:04:36.990
"She wanted to see you, but you were sleeping.

56
00:04:36.991 --> 00:04:44.897
She says you saved Minnie May's life, and she's sorry she acted the way she did in the affair with the wine.

57
00:04:44.898 --> 00:04:49.369
She hopes you'll forgive her and be good friends with Diana again.

58
00:04:49.370 --> 00:04:52.087
You can go over there this evening if you like.

59
00:04:52.088 --> 00:04:55.911
Now, Anne, don't fly into the air!"

60
00:04:55.912 --> 00:05:00.268
The warning was needed because Anne instantly sprang to her feet.

61
00:05:00.269 --> 00:05:06.506
"Oh Marilla, can I go and see Diana right now without washing my dishes?

62
00:05:06.507 --> 00:05:08.430
I'll wash them when I come back.

63
00:05:08.431 --> 00:05:14.707
I can't do something so unromantic as dishwashing at this thrilling moment."

64
00:05:14.708 --> 00:05:20.626
"Yes, yes, run along," said Marilla indulgently, smiling.

65
00:05:20.627 --> 00:05:25.912
Anne ran through the orchard to the Barrys', not caring about the wind or cold.

66
00:05:25.913 --> 00:05:32.573
Mrs. Barry kissed her and cried, and said she was sorry and that she could never repay Anne.

67
00:05:32.574 --> 00:05:37.555
Anne was embarrassed but replied politely, "I forgive you, Mrs. Barry.

68
00:05:37.556 --> 00:05:42.473
I can tell you again that I did not mean to make Diana drunk."

69
00:05:42.474 --> 00:05:45.729
Diana and Anne had a lovely afternoon.

70
00:05:45.730 --> 00:05:49.947
Diana showed Anne a new crochet stitch her aunt had taught her.

71
00:05:49.948 --> 00:05:56.034
Then Diana gave Anne a beautiful card with a wreath of roses on it and a verse of poetry:

72
00:05:56.035 --> 00:06:01.708
"If you love me as I love you, nothing but death can part us two."

73
00:06:01.709 --> 00:06:12.973
At school Diana and Anne sat together again, and they were the happiest girls in Avonlea.

